\[
 \Pi_\mu(h;\rho)
 =\operatorname{Tr}\rho\left[
       J_\mu^*hJ_\mu-\tfrac12\{R_\mu,h\}\right]
 =\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}\rho J_\mu^*[h,J_\mu].        \tag{14}
\]
U is an unnormalized output-energy contribution. Pi is the selected dissipative contribution to the ordinary-energy derivative when that derivative is defined. These are not interchangeable with a measured heat, reservoir energy loss, or photon absorption.

Put Delta_2 f(n)=f(n+2)-f(n). Spectral calculus and (1) give the bounded identities
