\[
 \mathcal L_f^*(F)=\sum_\mu R_\mu\Delta_2 f(N).                   \tag{22}
\]
The mild integral identity therefore holds for EVERY initial density without any electric-moment assumption:
\[
 \langle F\rangle_t-\langle F\rangle_0
   =\int_0^t\sum_\mu
            \langle R_\mu\Delta_2 f(N)\rangle_s\,ds.             \tag{23}
\]
This is the exact bounded difference contribution to any legitimate full-energy balance; it is not a proof that the full unbounded energy balance always exists.

